# Notebook outputs: a decision to make deliberately, once.
#
# By default git stores whatever is in the .ipynb, which includes every rendered figure
# and printed table. That has a real upside — GitHub renders notebooks inline, so a reader
# sees your figures and numbers without your data or your analysis stack — and two real
# costs: diffs are large and unreadable, and the repository grows on every re-run.
#
# It is also a DISCLOSURE decision. Committed outputs publish whatever the notebook
# printed. If your data is sensitive and your repository is or may become public, strip
# them:
#
#     pip install nbstripout
#     nbstripout --install --attributes .gitattributes
#
# which adds a filter here and clears outputs on commit. If instead you want outputs
# committed, say so here so the next person knows it was chosen rather than overlooked.
#
# This template commits them: the example notebook is meant to be read on GitHub.
*.ipynb diff=ipynb
